Package: jacarandr
Title: Colour Palettes Inspired by the Jacaranda Tree
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jazon", email = "67318977+jazon7@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Colour palettes inspired by the violet blooms of the
    jacaranda tree and the Australian trees that flower alongside it in late
    spring. Provides an eight colour discrete palette checked for
    distinguishability under simulated colour vision deficiency, a lighter
    companion palette, a sequential light to dark jacaranda palette and a
    diverging jacaranda to fig leaf palette. Includes helpers to retrieve and
    preview the colours in base R graphics, and discrete and continuous
    scales for 'ggplot2' with a consistent way to reverse any palette.
